invariant: INV-50
file: sha512_compress_blocks.c
catches: sha2_equiv_test
reason: load_block reads the block's third word into the ring's second
  place as well as its third, so the block's second word never enters
  the hash, and two messages that differ in those eight bytes alone have
  one digest. Each step the proofs hold still computes FIPS 180-4's value
  from what it is given, because the proofs take any ring: the load and
  the order of the calls rest on bin/sha2_equiv_test, whose first case
  with a second word differs from the reference.

--- old
    ring[1] = load_word(p + 8);
--- new
    ring[1] = load_word(p + 16);
